37. Application vs Infrastructure Coupling

The agent must distinguish:

Application OS Coupling

from:

Infrastructure OS Coupling

Example:

Deployment script:

yum install package-x

This may be infrastructure coupling rather than application runtime coupling.

Example:

Application:

subprocess.run(["yum", "install", "package-x"])

This is application OS coupling.

38. Intentional OS Coupling

OS coupling is not automatically an architecture violation.

Example:

Application
    ↓
RHEL

may be acceptable when:

RHEL is an enterprise standard

Application is certified for supported RHEL versions

OS upgrades are tested

No unsupported OS internals are used

Dependency is documented

Upgrade path exists

Report:

Intentional / Acceptable OS Coupling

when appropriate.

