40. Severity Model

LOW

Portable dependency. OS change normally does not require application changes.

Examples:

Standard filesystem APIs

Container-internal paths

Standard sockets

Standard runtime APIs

Platform-managed configuration

MEDIUM

OS change may require configuration, runtime, deployment, or compatibility changes.

Examples:

Specific runtime version

Specific OS package

Hardcoded application path

Native library with documented compatibility

OS-specific environment variable

HIGH

Application strongly depends on OS implementation or behavior.

Examples:

Host filesystem

OS-specific API

OS-specific command

systemd dependency

Specific ABI

Kubernetes hostPath

OS-specific security policy

OS-specific native library

CRITICAL

Application fundamentally depends on kernel, hardware, privileged host access, or low-level platform behavior.

Examples:

Kernel module

Host device

Docker socket

Kernel-specific behavior

Privileged host access

