46. Evidence Rules

The agent must distinguish between:

Observed Evidence

and:

Inference

Example:

Observed:
Application reads /etc/myapp/config.

Observed:
Dockerfile creates /etc/myapp/config.

Inference:
The path is container-internal.

Conclusion:
Host OS coupling = LOW.

Do not state HIGH OS coupling unless evidence establishes that the dependency belongs to the host OS or relies on OS-specific behavior.

47. Confidence

HIGH

Use HIGH when:

Direct source-code evidence exists

Configuration explicitly establishes the dependency

Multiple repositories corroborate the dependency

Runtime configuration confirms the dependency

Host/OS boundary is explicit

MEDIUM

Use MEDIUM when:

Dependency is strongly indicated

Only one evidence source exists

Runtime context is incomplete

Dependency ownership is unclear

LOW

Use LOW when:

Dependency is inferred

Evidence is incomplete

OS ownership cannot be established

Repository context is missing

When evidence is insufficient:

Status = REQUIRES_VALIDATION

Do not convert an inference into a fact.

